in a society there are rules some rules  serve as laws like don't kill or steal  others function as social norms like  don't chew with your mouth open or pick  your nose in public but some are much  more nuanced some social rules aren't so  much rules but are more like  expectations and standards like knowing  how to behave in different environments  with different people like knowing who  you are which you are good at and where  you stand in various social hierarchies  and then acting accordingly like knowing  how to assess people's reactions to you  and adapting appropriately and when  someone does the wrong thing related to  one of these types of rules and acts in  a way that is oblivious and detached  from what is socially expected they're  not arrested and they are typically not  even scolded but something else  interesting happens when someone behaves  in a way that demonstrates a lack of  understanding and awareness of both  themselves in the context of society  that they are in the people observing  this individual experience a weird  phenomenon a phenomenon that's often  described as cringing a feeling of  embarrassment and pain for the other  person the videos photos music and  real-life experiences that make us coil  up and feel a tightening sensation the  instances that can make us feel horrible  for someone but kind of good about  ourselves at the same time the things  that can inherently be sad but for some  reason still tend to make us laugh  there's a weird enjoyment found in the  sensation of cringing so much so that a  huge category of humor and entertainment  is rooted in the experience of it but  why what is it about seeing someone else  do something weird wrong or embarrassing  that is so enjoyable firstly before we  answer this we should understand why we  feel the sensation in the first place  cringing is a result of an empathetic  function known as vicarious  embarrassment where an observer  empathizes with and feels embarrassment  for another person it is a response  caused by mirror neurons which are  neurons that fire when someone observes  someone else and imagines him or herself  in their shoes the cringe we feel when  watching someone breaches social  expectation and do something  embarrassing is similar to how one might  feel when seeing someone break a bone or  get a bad cut as it activates the same  part of the brain known as the pain  matrix when seeing someone else get hurt  the observer can often experience a  cringe like response as their brand  attempts to self impose the sensation in  order to effectively empathize with the  individual they are observing this  effect allows us to feel bad for others  to care about how others feel and to  function smoothly as a society we  everyone always hurting each other  however in terms of experiencing a  cringe because of someone else's  behavior it takes more than just doing  something embarrassing to be considered  cringy things like tripping in front of  a lot of people farting in the middle of  a meeting or spilling a drink on oneself  while trying to take a sip are all  certainly embarrassing but they are not  really cringey this is because they  don't contain an essential factor  something that is cringy requires a  person intentionally doing an  embarrassing action paired with a lack  of awareness that their action is in  fact even embarrassing they lack  self-awareness and furthermore they lack  awareness of the people and context  around them they have at least in this  situation what is known as a weak theory  of mind which is the psychological  ability to accurately discern one's self  from others they don't understand that  others are seeing the world differently  than them and there's no connective  tissue between how they think they are  coming off and how they are actually  coming off the person tripping in front  of a crowd did not mean or want a trip  interpreting does not suggest the lack  of self or social awareness because the  person tripping is typically aware that  it is somewhat embarrassing and responds  accordingly similarly with the other  examples making a mistake in doing  something embarrassing does not always  equal something that is indicative of  cringing perhaps it may be funny but not  always cringy examples of things that  are indicative of cringing are things  more like the singer who thinks they are  so good that they go on a national TV  talent show to perform only to turn out  being awful and ridiculed by the judges  the man who is extremely confident in  approaching a woman only to ask her out  and be harshly rejected the person who  thinks they are cool or tough in a  certain way and post something boastful  online will need to look insecure and  weak the comedian who thinks their joke  is funny but it falls flat in front of a  confused audience  no you are all all left all of these  examples contain the same principle  someone thinks of themselves in a  certain way often involving the belief  that they possess a certain skillset  then presents that sense of self in a  social context but is completely wrong  and comes off weird foolish unskilled  and/or detached from reality and when we  see this it makes us feel that cringing  sensation  I'm morbid peek into the mind of a  person who is so far out of touch that  it makes us feel pain for them but the  most fascinating question that cringing  raises is why would anyone enjoy  watching this why would the act of  observing someone flop over themselves  so miserably and so publicly be  pleasurable in life it is inevitable  that we experience things that are  awkward embarrassing and perhaps even  cringy in our own personal life we will  mess up or not be as good as we thought  we were in something we will do  something weird out of nervousness we  will learn something new and realize how  little we knew about the world only a  short time before we will feel like we  have no idea what's going on in certain  situations and that we are strange and  detached but we will hate all of this  and we will fear it and in order to  combat it we will live our life  attempting to prove to the world that we  are good composed and not weird at all  we will perform for others we will study  and examine the various social context  that we pass through building our  knowledge and understanding of how to  best perform so that we fit smoothly  into the various templates of normality  but we will know deep down that even if  we are successful in our performances  for the world we will be lying to  ourselves  that the things that society might deem  embarrassing or wrong we sometimes do  but sometimes we don't really know who  we are or how to act that we might know  what we are good at but are never really  sure of how good and if people really  like us or what we do that sometimes we  feel kind of lost like an infant being  put in the center of a corn maze and  told to find their way out and when we  watch someone else try to perform and  impress others only to end up doing  something that is so far off and weird  something that is so lacking in social  and self-awareness we realize that one's  own weirdness and uncertainty is  relatively speaking pretty normal  thank you for watching if we found  enjoyment and value in this video please  give it a thumbs up share your thoughts  in the comments below and if you are not  already be sure to subscribe to our  Channel  we are constantly coming out with new  videos to help you experience life with  clarity and Wonder
 

